2026-09-27T10:19:12.3482080Z Description:
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3482673Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3483221Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3484826Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3486440Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3486598Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3486943Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3487393Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3487713Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3487816Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3488086Z ================
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3488229Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3488402Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3488821Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3489073Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3489200Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3489515Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3489710Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3489867Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3490310Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3490717Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3491493Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3492124Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3492242Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3492734Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3493360Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3493917Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3494220Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3494632Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3494721Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3494932Z ========
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3495047Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3496303Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3497598Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3497809Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3498274Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3499051Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3499626Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3500167Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3564240Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3565132Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3565346Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3565862Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3566171Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3567882Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3569900Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3571101Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3572660Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:19:12.3573063Z 
